ical agents, budget 25 split equally, no mint, no validation · measure: all of hardest level, targets solved, bounty value, ROI, knowledge found (bits), knowledge per unit of money, money to the main level, waste · 30 runs per row.</p>\n<p><strong>Caveats:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A simulation with guessed parameters: it shows how the rules play out, not that they work.</li>\n</ul>\n<details><summary>Details</summary><p>The simple model on a generated idea graph (4 levels × 6 ideas, 1.5 parents each, sequences of 2 bits growing by 1 per level, composition 0.7); each run draws its own graph. Only α and β vary. Held fixed: 12 identical agents, a budget of 25 split equally every round (f = 0), no flat mint, a knowledge reward of 1 per new bit flowing back with α, no validation.</p>\n<p>Values are mean ± standard deviation over runs.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>society</th>\n<th>budget</th>\n<th>frontier</th>\n<th>targets solved</th>\n<th>value gained</th>\n<th>ROI (value per spend)</th>\n<th>knowledge (bits)</th>\n<th>knowledge published (bits)</th>\n<th>bits per money</th>\n<th>cost</th>\n<th>waste</th>\n<th>sharing</th>\n<th>reach L4</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>0.1 ± 0.7</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.2</td>\n<td>1 ± 6</td>\n<td>0.04 ± 0.24</td>\n<td>8 ± 2</td>\n<td>0 ± 1</td>\n<td>0.314 ± 0.100</td>\n<td>12 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.34 ± 0.15</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.03</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>0.5 ± 1.4</td>\n<td>0.1 ± 0.3</td>\n<td>4 ± 11</td>\n<td>0.09 ± 0.23</td>\n<td>11 ± 3</td>\n<td>1 ± 2</td>\n<td>0.235 ± 0.060</td>\n<td>36 ± 17</td>\n<td>0.46 ± 0.13</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>2.0 ± 2.0</td>\n<td>0.6 ± 0.6</td>\n<td>18 ± 20</td>\n<td>0.19 ± 0.22</td>\n<td>17 ± 3</td>\n<td>3 ± 4</td>\n<td>0.180 ± 0.037</td>\n<td>65 ± 23</td>\n<td>0.59 ± 0.10</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.50</